{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794234544,"nonce":"F5n4skc1fzj4WssemAV4vqraNzU=","title":"An integer index on a per-point vector Variable slices the points, not a component","message":"A Variable holding a per-point vector (n_q, n) indexed as w[1] goes through Placeholder.__getitem__, which builds x[k] and so picks quadrature point 1 instead of component 1. The value is silently wrong; only x[..., i] takes a component. Found on the face-operator symbol S(trace), whose own __getitem__ now takes a component; other per-point Variables (context-backed coefficient fields) still slice the points.\n\nReproduce: a boundary term reading S(tE).x[1] before the fix gave a wrong TE admittance (the exact face reflected more than the first-order one); with S(tE).x[..., 1] or the fixed indexing it converges at second order (tests/test_fem_face_operator.py::test_maxwell_exact_face_transmits_te_and_tm).","files":null}]}